{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested for exact a4c62f0f3a965bbba00ebc3e1d468ff8d031c521 (tree 3ac754acc01ec5af125e43a7adfca91ad1aab5dd), against Main afe0c319.\n\nThe two findings in ed3092c2 are addressed: reads/eligible now distinguish bounded candidate queries from party/related-item checks and incomplete coverage; admission now names B1 accept then B2 take-hold, plus durable team-object rows with key/generation/lease for P1/P2/C1 and race/restart witnesses. The reservation.ts citation is corrected.\n\nOne remaining P2: B2 must distinguish abandoned work from work already reported (notes/2026-10-21-roles-flow-and-instances.md:148). Its complete stated eligibility is an accepted commitment owned by this member, with no held hold. But report opens a separate report and does not change the accepted commitment (issue.ts:552-591); accept-report also changes only the report (issue.ts:592-613). Holds can be released or expire while the report awaits requester judgment or the owner's review/merge (shared.ts:145-156, 177-182). At that point B2 admits another instance to the same commitment and tells it to open another change, rebuild and report again. The handoff no longer leaves work waiting for the next role; it can repeatedly restart already delivered work.\n\nRead/reconcile reports under the commitment as part of B2 eligibility. Define the waiting state after a report, how an accepted report remains handed off, and what explicit refusal or retry decision makes fresh builder work eligible. Preserve sibling recovery for an expired/lost-key assignment that has not reported. A durable host disposition may participate, but the report in the app must be recovered after restart rather than forgotten. Add a witness: submit a report; release/expire the hold; run two builder instances and restart the host; no new builder assignment/change appears while the report is reported or accepted. Separately show the intended retry after refusal.\n\nSmall clarification while editing: directory index rows are item type lane in item state listed; issue/pr and open/closed are value slots (packages/platform/src/directory.ts:196-214). Spell those as the initial candidate query plus eligibility filters, rather than suggesting type issue/state open are the directory query. The candidate lane scope should be read for current state and coverage; an index is advisory.\n\nRead primary affd4c37 first in full: 372 lines / 21026 bytes / SHA256 be6854048c4e0ebf16e236ea0b9bf4042a1742947ece48e0ab49d75b5db1da0a. Then reviewed the complete agent-teams amendment against the previously fully read draft 1: only the three added admission-record lines change; its 718-line / 45208-byte current blob is SHA256 524a17fd28a16168c37100bfea609ab0229c9ac2c93215897a703f4ccad738ba. Native reporting order aac77f30 then affd4c37 is the actual implementation-report binding, while reading order remains primary first. Both fresh Sources are included; old draft Sources are retired, and the older Main team-note predecessor remains live pending landing succession.\n\nSame-member/more-keys, authority, membership enrollment, review independence, Counter behavior and RI slice order remain as previously checked. Design review only. Fourteen current copied design/code blobs and modes matched immutable Git; only the two declared note paths differ from Main. git diff --check afe0c319 a4c62f0f passed. No tests/gate, installation, shared source edits, WIP execution, deployment or publication. Evidence root closed before filing.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:aac77f30b20ad573e537e1e5cb9b350afc6b429a","binding":"assigned","head":"a4c62f0f3a965bbba00ebc3e1d468ff8d031c521","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:b7ef07bc63c8a7e3ede54473123f4fe30bf9790f\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:ed60b27298e1e0b46a7b9bf26bece0ae651854e0\"]","review_frontier":"gi